BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260402T200000Z
DTEND:20260402T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260402T000000Z
SUMMARY:Laser Cut Your Own Acrylic Phone Stand
DESCRIPTION:Join the Maker   STEAM team to use the laser cutter to engrave 
 and cut an acrylic phone stand in a small group learning environment with 
 hands-on help! We will use our materials and provide materials for one 
 acrylic phone stand per registrant. Come ready with a roughly 2" x 2" 
 engrave design idea\, a .jpg or .png of your design image via cloud 
 storage\, or just curiosity and we will have a few templates to choose from 
 as well.\n\nThis small-group atmosphere will help introduce you to the 
 laser cutter in a welcoming setting and show you the process of completing 
 a laser cut project to help you prepare for when you reserve the laser 
 cutter on your own in the future.\n\nRegistration is required. Participants 
 will need to sign a safety waiver when in the makerspace. (This program is 
 open to teens and adults. Teens under the age of 18 must have a 
 guardian/parent present to sign the waiver.)\n\nWe also ask that you take 
 the online\, self-paced laser cutter orientation prior to coming to the 
 program (if you haven't already) so that the orientation setup steps are 
 completed.\n\nNote: If you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:High & Low Sensory Stimulation, Innovation Lab, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16526850
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16526850
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260402T204000Z
DTEND:20260402T214000Z
DTSTAMP:20260402T000000Z
SUMMARY:Reading Time with Ms. Chloe
DESCRIPTION:Registration Required. To schedule a time\, go to: Make an 
 Appointment - DCoL Events & Room Reservations - Durham County 
 Library\n\nDoes your child need more reading practice and could benefit 
 from more reading aloud time? Or are they just learning phonics sounds and 
 need more practice to build blending skills? Then this program is for them! 
 Schedule a 20-minute session for your child with Ms. Chloe to work together 
 with your child on reading and blending practice. You’re welcome to bring 
 your own book or I’ll pull some books that will work for their range. 
 \n\nWhile parents/ guardians don’t have to attend\, they must remain on 
 the children’s floor while their child is attending their session.\n\nFor 
 more information\, contact: chloebullock@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Library - Children's Area\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chloe Bullock":MAILTO:chloebullock@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16591700
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16591700
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260402T230000Z
DTEND:20260403T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260402T000000Z
SUMMARY:Triangle Comics Creator Network
DESCRIPTION:Tons of comics writers and artists make their homes in Durham\, 
 Chapel Hill\, Raleigh\, Hillsborough\, Cary and nearby\, but too many of us 
 think we're alone. Well\, not anymore!  Join the Triangle Comics Creator 
 Network and get to know fellow creators of all backgrounds\, working in all 
 genres\, at all skill levels.  Friends and family welcome too.\n\nThis 
 month we will have a comics critique! Please bring any works you want 
 feedback on.\n\nHope to see you there!\n\nWe will be meeting at Atomic 
 Empire\, located at the following address:\n\n3400 Westgate Dr 
 #14b\n\nDurham\, NC 27707\n\nLearn more about the group and RSVP through 
 our Meetup page.\n\nHave questions? Want to hear more about the anthology? 
 Feel free to call Mara (she/her/hers) at 919-560-0207 or email her at 
 mplantholt@dconc.gov.
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16381619
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16381619
END:VEVENT
