DTEND:20260407T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T000000Z
SUMMARY:Grandparenting Autism
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a warm\, informative session designed especially 
 for grandparents. Together\, we’ll explore what autism is\, acknowledge 
 the hopes and dreams that come with grandparenting\, and discuss how those 
 experiences may look different when supporting a grandchild on the autism 
 spectrum. Participants will learn practical\, compassionate ways to build 
 meaningful connections with their grandchild and discover helpful 
 strategies for supporting their adult children as parents. This program 
 offers guidance\, understanding\, and a welcoming space for questions and 
 shared experiences.\n\nIf you have any questions\, please contact Chelsea 
 Romero (cromero@dconc.gov) or Cindy Martin (cmartin@autismsociety-nc.org)
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
