DTSTART:20260408T220000Z
DTEND:20260408T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260408T000000Z
SUMMARY:Rescheduled date -> Home Repair Lab Special Edition: How to Fix a Leak
DESCRIPTION:This program is the rescheduled date from Monday\, March 16th. 
 Please note the new date and time\, and please re-register for your 
 spot.\n\nJoin Chris and Mindy Meyers from Home Repair Lab for an exclusive 
 class at their shop! This class will include lecture information\, followed 
 by some hands-on practice and Q&A.\n\nIn this month's program\, we'll be 
 joined by staff with the City of Durham Water Department for a special 
 program for Fix a Leak Week! City of Durham staff will kick off the 
 program\, then participants will learn how to fix basic leaks with Chris 
 and Mindy. Relevant for homeowners\, first time home buyers\, and renters. 
 Registration is required\, and participants will sign a safety waiver for 
 Home Repair Lab. Home Repair Lab is located at 803 Ramseur St Suite E\, 
 Durham\, NC 27701.\n\nNote: This program is a repeat of content from last 
 year\, so if you attend last year\, you will not need to attend 
 again.\n\n*Special note: This program is offsite and the building is not 
 ADA-complient. If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation 
 needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all 
 requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to ensure we 
 can provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16594000
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16594000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260408T220000Z
DTEND:20260408T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260408T000000Z
SUMMARY:Wednesday Computer Class @ Main
DESCRIPTION:Come join a supportive group environment for self-paced digital 
 skills courses. We'll be using Northstar Digital Literacy\, a free online 
 resource available to all Durham County Library patrons. A library staff 
 member will be present to get you set up and answer questions as each 
 participant moves through online modules on their own at their own pace. 
 Northstar allows you to track your learning progress and earn badges or 
 certificates for completing a course. These classes are best for learners 
 who have at least basic keyboard and mouse skills. Our computer lab has a 
 limited number of laptops for use\, so bringing your own laptop and 
 headphones is encouraged.\n\nComputer and digital skills topics 
 include:\n\n\n	Phone Keyboard Basics & Logging In\n	Basic Computer 
 Skills\n	Internet Basics\n	Using Email\n	Windows 10 & 11\n	Mac 
 OS\n	Microsoft Word\, Excel\, and PowerPoint\n	Google Docs\n	Social 
 Media\n	Information Literacy\n	Career Search Skills\n	Your Digital 
 Footprint\n	Accessing Telehealth Appointments\n	Cybersecurity 
 Basics\n\n\nThese classes are self-paced and each week participants will 
 choose which lessons they want to complete on their own. You do not need to 
 have come to the first class to attend the following weeks and there is no 
 requirement to commit to all of the classes through April. Register for the 
 weeks that work best for you!\n\nIf you have any questions or accommodation 
 needs\, contact Jimmy McKinnell at jmckinnell@dconc.gov or call 
 919-560-9940
LOCATION:Computer Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Computer Class, Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16276912
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16276912
END:VEVENT
