SUMMARY:Spring Sensory Bins @ Southwest
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to try sensory bins at home\, but are 
 intimidated by the set up or mess? Join Southwest's children's staff for an 
 hour of outdoor exploratory play and fun\, then let us clean up! Sensory 
 bins are a great way to expose your child to different textures\, engage 
 their senses\, increase socialization with peers\, and improve fine motor 
 skills. \n\nThis program is geared towards children ages 2 . Please note 
 that this program will have a mix of taste-safe activities and bins with 
 small filler items such as rice\, pasta\, etc. \n\nQuestions? Please email 
 Kristen @ kstockdale@dconc.gov or call (919) 560-8592.
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Outdoor Space\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:High & Low Sensory Stimulation, Other, Sensory Friendly, Social
