SUMMARY:Open Sew with Connecting with Threads
DESCRIPTION:If you know how to use a sewing machine and to do basic hand 
 sewing\, join Connecting with Threads to create your own projects in our 
 "Open Sew" series. This is a series of programs where teens and tweens will 
 be able to continue to build their knowledge as independent sewers.  You 
 will be provided a list of projects you can work on for yourself or use one 
 of our kits to create a bag\, a pillowcase\, a quilt or other item to give 
 back to our community!  All items created for the community will be donated 
 through a local nonprofit organization to reach our community members who 
 need them.\n\nThere are other dates in this series\, including Apr 11\, Apr 
 25\, May 9\, May 23\, June 6 and June 20. This program is for teens and 
 tweens ages 9 and up! Registration is required!
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline P.":MAILTO:cbpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts
