SUMMARY:Emerging Trends in End of Life Care  [POSTPONED TO APRIL 15]
DESCRIPTION:This presentation will offer a comprehensive look at the 
 evolving landscape of end-of-life choices\, from eco-friendly burial 
 practices to aquamation and human composting. Participants will explore the 
 importance of proactive decision-making—from legal documents and advance 
 directives to thoughtful conversations with loved ones. Hunter Beattie\, 
 owner of Endswell\, will highlight how sustainable\, personalized\, and 
 community-centered approaches are reshaping modern death care\, empowering 
 individuals to leave a meaningful legacy that honors both personal values 
 and the environment.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Gardening
