SUMMARY:Home Fundamentals with Home Repair Lab
DESCRIPTION:Join Chris and Mindy Meyers from Home Repair Lab to learn about 
 home fundamentals! This lecture-focused class will help you understand how 
 your home operates\, give you knowledge to interact with service 
 providers\, and be your own advocate. Relevant for homeowners\, first time 
 home buyers\, and renters. The first hour will be lecture\, followed by 
 Q&A. \n\nMore detailed class description:\n\nHome Fundamentals helps you 
 understand the systems that provide comfort and safety in a home\, 
 structural\, plumbing and electrical. You'll learn technique\, terminology 
 and materials used to build each system.  \n\n\n	Structural explores 
 foundations\, framing\, roofs\, structural load\, drywall and lots more.  
 \n	Pluming examines rural water/waste vs. city water/waste as well as the 
 materials and fixtures that supply water and remove waste from the home.  
 \n	Electrical sheds light on how power is brought to and distributed 
 throughout a home\, from panels and sub-panels to circuits\, breakers\, 
 receptacles and appliances.\n\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-15946800
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15946800
END:VEVENT
