DTSTAMP:20260416T000000Z
SUMMARY:Game Night for Science: Stall Catchers! (Citizen Science Month)
DESCRIPTION:Game Night for Science: Play Stall Catchers Online\n\nApril 
 16\, 2026 at 2pm ET\n\nTurn game night into real scientific impact! 
 \n\nJoin us in-person as we learn how to play an online game to analyze 
 data and help scientists better understand Alzheimer’s disease. The 
 project scientist from Cornell will join us via Zoom to describe the 
 research and answer any questions as we participate in “Stall 
 Catchers\,” together. \n\nJoin us and be part of 2.50 Million Acts of 
 Science this April during Citizen Science Month. No experience 
 needed—just curiosity! \n\nPlease bring a device (phone\, laptop\, or 
 tablet) if you can. Limited devices are available.
LOCATION:South Meeting Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaris Torres":MAILTO:amaristorres@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Community Engagement, Digital/Tech Literacy, Gaming, Health & Fitness, Social, STEAM
