SUMMARY:Author Talk with Chrystal Mitchell
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the North Regional Library for a special author talk 
 with Chrystal Mitchell\, featuring her book I Can Do ALL 
 Things.\n\nChrystal will share insights from documenting thirty days of her 
 son’s autism and ADHD journey\, offering an honest look at his 
 behaviors\, sensory needs\, daily routines\, and strategies that help 
 reduce anxiety and support learning. Her message reminds families that they 
 are not alone and that consistency and community make a meaningful 
 difference.\n\n \n\n \n\nA book signing with the author will take place 
 immediately after the program.\n\n\n\n \n\nApril is recognized as Autism 
 Awareness Month\, a time dedicated to increasing understanding\, promoting 
 acceptance\, and supporting individuals and families affected by autism. 
 \n\nThis program is open to all.
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kathleen Hayes":MAILTO:khayes@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement, Homeschool
