BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260418T180000Z
DTEND:20260418T191500Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T000000Z
SUMMARY:Period Talk: A Guide for Dads & Allies
DESCRIPTION:Menstruation is a natural part of life—but it’s not always 
 a topic everyone feels prepared to talk about. This welcoming and 
 judgment-free program is designed especially for dads\, caregivers\, and 
 allies who want to better understand and support the people in their lives 
 who menstruate.\n\nParticipants will learn the basics of menstruation\, 
 including what to expect\, how to talk about it openly\, and how to provide 
 practical and emotional support. We’ll explore common products\, answer 
 frequently asked questions\, and break down myths and stigmas surrounding 
 periods.\n\nWhether you’re a dad wanting to support your child\, a 
 caregiver looking to learn\, or simply someone who wants to be a better 
 advocate\, this session offers the tools\, language\, and confidence to 
 show up with understanding and care.\n\nIf you have any accessibility 
 questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us at cromero@dconc.gov. 
 We ask that all requests be made at least three (3) business days prior to 
 the event to ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16613968
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16613968
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260418T190000Z
DTEND:20260418T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T000000Z
SUMMARY:Period Party: Pack Your Power Pouch
DESCRIPTION:Let’s turn period prep into a party! Join us for a fun\, 
 creative\, and welcoming Period Party where participants will design and 
 assemble their own personal period pouches.\n\nThese handy pouches can be 
 filled with essentials like pads\, tampons\, wipes\, and other comfort 
 items—perfect for keeping in a backpack\, locker\, or car. While we 
 craft\, we’ll also have open\, stigma-free conversations about 
 menstruation\, body literacy\, and how to support ourselves and others with 
 confidence and care.\n\nThis program is open to anyone who menstruates\, 
 supports someone who does\, or simply wants to learn more. All supplies 
 will be provided—just bring your creativity!\n\nIf you have any 
 accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us at 
 cromero@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least three (3) 
 business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best 
 accommodations possible!
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16613972
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16613972
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260418T190000Z
DTEND:20260418T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T000000Z
SUMMARY:This Week In the Lab: Paper Crafts
DESCRIPTION:Join the STEAM Team in the Innovation Lab during specified open 
 hours to do paper crafts by creating your own Zine and fold 
 origami!\n\nZines (pronounced "zeens") are tough to define because they can 
 be so many things! Basically\, they are self-published\nbooklets containing 
 anything you want - art\, writing\, drawings\, recipes\, poetry\, comics\, 
 etc. The content and look\nare totally up to the creator. It's all about 
 self-expression. Origami is an ancient art technique to fold paper into 
 exciting and unexpected shapes.\n\nThis is a self-paced activity. You can 
 drop in during the listed Open Lab Hours.\n\nInnovation Lab Open 
 Hours:\n\nMonday: Closed\nTuesday: 1pm - 5pm\nWednesday: closed (*different 
 this week)\nThursday: 10am - 2pm\nFriday: 1pm - 5pm\nSaturday: 3pm - 5pm 
 (*different this week)\n\nHours subject to change based on staffing and 
 programming needs.
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16218211
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16218211
END:VEVENT
