SUMMARY:Quilted Stories Project with Tweens
DESCRIPTION:With guidance from the local non-profit group\, Connecting with 
 Threads\, children ages 9 to 12 will learn how to make -- and to 
 personalize -- a quilted block. The pieces will be assembled for exhibition 
 during a presentation with local author and long-time quilter\, Frances 
 O'Roark Dowell\, the following Saturday (April 25\, from 3:00 to 4:00) at 
 Southwest Regional. Each participant will also receive an additional sewing 
 kit with everything needed to make a quilted block at 
 home.\n\n*Reservations required. Adult supervision also advised.\n\nFor 
 ages 9 through 12 ONLY (slots for 20 children available)
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Olivia Singleton":MAILTO:osingleton@dconc.gov
