DTSTAMP:20260420T000000Z
SUMMARY:Paperhand Puppet Project presents "A World of Wonder!"
DESCRIPTION:Paperhand Puppet Project presents:\n\n"A World of Wonder!” 
 \n\n \n\n\nA whimsical and interactive showcasing of creatures and 
 characters from Paperhand’s 26 year history that celebrates the wild 
 wisdom of our world.\n\n\nMeet a myriad of magical and grand oversized 
 animals\, all made in Paperhand studio in Saxapahaw NC\, brought to life by 
 puppeteers for all ages to enjoy.\n\n\nAll the masks and puppets move and 
 dance to music as they engage\, inspire and incite joy. Join us for this 
 super fun performance with an award winning troupe\, that’s sure to 
 delight.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPaperhand Puppet Project is a North Carolina-based 
 nonprofit performing arts organization whose mission is to create art that 
 inspires connection. By practicing\, performing and teaching the art of 
 puppetry\, we strive to nurture the best in humanity\, build creative 
 culture\, and help celebrate and protect the natural world. \n\n 
 \n\nFeaturing 2 shows as a part of Library Fest 2026 on Monday\, April 20\, 
 2026 in the Main Library Auditorium at 11:00 a.m. and 1:00 
 p.m.\n\nRegistration is preferred. Please make sure you register from the 
 correct page for your preferred time slot.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhere can I park when 
 the Main Library parking lot is full?\n\nParking is available in the 
 library parking lot or at the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 
 North Queen Street which is behind the apartments directly across the 
 street from the library. Parking is free in the garage. Please bring your 
 ticket to a service desk in the library for validation.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Celeste Holtzmann":MAILTO:choltzmann@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Durham Library Foundation, Library Fest
UID:LibCal-14288-16605028
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/calendar/14288/paperhands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260420T150000Z
DTEND:20260420T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20260420T000000Z
SUMMARY:Turn your Memories into Poems
DESCRIPTION:Join Durham's Poet Laureate\, Chris Vitiello\, for a fun and 
 engaging workshop that will have you making poems out of your memories! 
 Whether or not you consider yourself a poet or writer\, come learn simple 
 techniques for turning personal memories into meaningful 
 (magical/expressive/heartfelt/delightfully quirky) poems. Expect 
 creativity\, conversation\, and plenty of inspiration. No experience 
 necessary--perfect for writers of all levels.\n\nWorkshop is 1 hour\, 
 followed by an optional 30 minute writing time.\n\n\na {\n    
 text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr th\, tr td {\n    
 border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    background-color: 
 #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\n\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: 
 #464feb\;\n}\ntr th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th 
 {\n    background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks to Durham Library 
 Foundation for their support of this event\, part of Library Fest 2026: The 
 Stories That Built US
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham Library Foundation, Humanities, Library Fest, Writing
UID:LibCal-14288-16618476
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16618476
END:VEVENT
