SUMMARY:Adult Story Time -- Sherlock Holmes
DESCRIPTION:Read-alouds are for grown-ups too! Join us for a weekday 
 evening adult story time at the North Regional Library. Flop on the carpet 
 with a floor pillow\, pull up a chair\, or sit at a table if you want to 
 bring your own dinner or snacks. Spend an hour listening to read-alouds 
 from books and stories in the library collection. Tea\, coffee\, and hot 
 chocolate will be provided.\n\nThis month: two short stories from a bulky 
 volume called The Improbable Adventures of Sherlock Holmes. This anthology 
 comprises tales by contemporary authors in the style of the original 
 stories with all the familiar details: the quarters at 221-B Baker Street\, 
 the spooky gaslit streets of London\, and "inexplicable" situations and 
 phenomena that will be handily navigated by Sherlock and Watson.\n\n(This 
 is the make-up session for January's snow cancellation.)\n\nRegistration is 
 appreciated but not required.\n\nE-mail Bob with any questions: 
 rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
